Wondering when to book wedding AV rentals in Malaga? We do not publish a fixed lead time, and be wary of anyone who quotes you one as a hard rule: what actually matters is that wedding dates, especially in peak season, and the technicians who work them fill up. Book once your date and venue are confirmed, and the earlier you do, the more likely your first choice date is still open. If you have not settled on a package yet, our [how to choose wedding rentals](/blog/how-to-choose-wedding-rentals/) guide walks through the six questions, starting with guest count, that decide between the Eco Pack and the Wedding Pack, before you get to timing your booking.

## Brief Overview

---

Malaga Event Gear's [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) covers the AV side of your day: PA sound for up to 80 guests, fairy light ambient lighting, wireless microphones for vows and speeches, and a live technician on site throughout. There is no minimum or maximum booking window, just availability, so reach out as soon as your date and venue are set.

## Key Highlights

---

-   No fixed lead time is required or published. Availability is what actually limits a date, not a rule.
-   Peak wedding season (spring through early autumn on the Costa del Sol) is when dates and technicians book out first.
-   The Wedding Pack includes a live technician on site, one of only two packages in our catalog that does.
-   Confirming your venue and date first is what lets us confirm equipment and technician availability for that day.

## Why There's No Fixed Booking Window

We don't ask couples to book a set number of months ahead, because the honest answer is that it depends on your date and the season. A weekday wedding in November has very different availability than a Saturday in June. What we can tell you is that once your venue and date are locked in, reaching out promptly is what protects your slot, particularly for the live technician, since the Wedding Pack and the MICE Pack are the only two in our catalog that include one.

